      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: ECONOMIC GROWTH (IN FULL DEPTH)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic Growth is a quantitative concept focusing on the continuous increase in real national income and GDP over time.",
        "Economic Development is a broader qualitative concept that includes economic growth along with structural, institutional, and social changes.",
        "Key indicators of economic development comprise Per Capita Income, health standards, literacy, and employment rates.",
        "Human Development Index (HDI) measures standard of living, knowledge, and health indicators for comprehensive developmental assessment.",
        "Sustainable Development emphasizes meeting present needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own."
      ],
      "id": "9q77adt"
    },
