    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinction between Growth and Development: Growth is purely quantitative (GDP/GNP), whereas Development includes qualitative socio-economic improvements.",
        "HDI Dimensions: Key components tested include Life Expectancy (Health), Schooling Years (Education), and GNI Per Capita (Standard of Living).",
        "Per Capita Income Formula: Total National Income divided by Total Population.",
        "Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs): Frequently asked in relation to resource conservation and environmental stability."
